WI-higik. pony.py names a type definition's kind after its node type,
so it emits `actor` and `primitive`, neither registered: the validator
flagged both (axis_conformance + id_format) on every Pony run. ADR-0027
register-vs-fold: REGISTERED (concrete type family), because pony also
emits `class` for its own class construct and a fold would fuse two
constructs. Registering changes no node.id and no stable_id. The schema,
concept-axes doc and a pony file in the schema-coverage corpus cover
them (the coverage baseline only shrinks: `static` is newly covered).
The strict xfail and the KIND_SLOT_HOLES entry for pony are removed.

WI-totam (c). slice's _CONTAINER_KINDS and the containment linker's
CONTAINER_KINDS were two hand-written copies, and slice's lacked
`object`: `slice --entry Registry --reverse` on a Kotlin object returned
only the object, where the same code as a class returned its members'
callers. Measured on 30 recent surveys, `object` was the source of
40,820 contains edges. Both now read symbol_kinds.container_kind_names():
the nominal type kinds plus SCOPE_CONTAINER_KINDS (file, module, type,
instance, message, library), so a newly registered type kind is a
container in both. The linker's set changes only by actor/primitive: on
a pony fixture, an actor's behaviour and a primitive's function now root
under them instead of under the file. `variable` stays out (a Go
variable has no members).

WI-totam (b): the concept-audit playbook's Step 4.5 header said "five"
producer-emit shapes while listing six.

Not done here: WI-totam (d) (no anchor-kind predicate) and (e) (JS
class-field initializers anchored on the file, a permitted divergence in
ADR-0023 awaiting its own measurement).

Addresses WI-higik, WI-totam.

